  "notes": "{冷|さ}ます is a transitive verb meaning to cool something down or let it cool.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{冷|さ}める→冷める：02114_sameru⟧ (intransitive, to cool down by itself)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {冷|さ}ます: to cool (temperature)\n- ⟦{覚|さ}ます→覚ます：02057_samasu⟧: to wake someone up\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦スープ→スープ：00395_suupu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|さ}ます: to cool the soup\n- ⟦{熱|ねつ}→熱：01690_netsu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|さ}ます: to bring down a fever\n- ⟦{頭|あたま}→頭：00574_atama⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|さ}ます: to cool one's head (calm down)\n- ⟦{興奮|こうふん}→興奮：02751_koufun⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|さ}ます: to calm excitement\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used metaphorically for cooling emotions or enthusiasm: ⟦{熱|ねつ}→熱：01690_netsu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{冷|さ}ます can mean to dampen enthusiasm.",
